      "message": "Could this be encapsulated into a macro to make it less error prone for future cases? Something like:\n```\nINDIRECT_HOOK(android_vh_add_page_to_lrulist,(folio, compound, lru) params),\n              (struct folio *folio, bool compound, enum lru_list lru));\n```\nWhich would be something like:\n```\n#define INDIRECT_HOOK(hook_name)\\\n  extern struct tracepoint __tracepoint_##hook_name;\\\n  void __trace_##hook_name args;\\\n  static __always_inline void _trace_##hook(params) {\\\n     if (static_key_false(\u0026__tracepoint_##hook_name.key))\\\n\t\t__trace_##hook_name args;\n```\nand would expand to:\n```\nextern struct tracepoint __tracepoint_android_vh_add_page_to_lrulist;\nvoid __trace_android_vh_add_page_to_lrulist(struct folio *folio, bool compound,\n\t\t\t\t\t    enum lru_list lru);\nstatic __always_inline void _trace_android_vh_add_page_to_lrulist(struct folio *folio, bool compound, enum lru_list lru)\n{\n\tif (static_key_false(\u0026__tracepoint_android_vh_add_page_to_lrulist.key))\n\t\t__trace_android_vh_add_page_to_lrulist(folio, compound, lru);\n}\n```",
